            <ArticleTitle>Non-planar oligoarylene macrocycles from biphenyl.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>11540-11543</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1039/c7cc06798d</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Saddle- and propeller-shaped macrocycles are obtained by fourfold Perkin condensations in transient high dilution of 4,4'-bis(phenylglyoxylic acid) with either 4,4'-bis(phenylacetic acid) or p-phenylenediacetic acid, followed by four-fold oxidative photocyclizations. In the saddle-shaped tetraphenanthrylene, the angle between opposite phenanthrene planes is close to the value of 90° of an ideal saddle. In the two helicene fragments of the propeller-shaped double [5]helicene, the geometry of unsubstituted [5]helicene is preserved without major macrocycle-induced distortions.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
